{title: 339 - God Is My Strong Salvation}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #339 • WIE LIEBLICH IST DER MAIEN • 7.6.7.6.D.}
{lyricist: James Montgomery}
{composer: J. Steurlein}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 339}
{meta: tune WIE LIEBLICH IST DER MAIEN}
{meta: meter 7.6.7.6.D.}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]God is [Eb]my [Bb]strong salvation,
[Cm]What [F]foe [Gm]have [F]I to [Bb]fear?
[Bb]In darkness and temptation,
[Cm]My [F]Light, [Gm]my [F]Help, is [Bb]near:
[Bb]Though hosts [Eb]encamp [Gm]around [F]me,
[Cm/Eb]Firm [Bb/D]in the [Cm]fight I stand;
[Bb/D]What [Eb]terror [Gm]can [Dm]confound [Eb]me,
[Eb]With [F]God [Bb/D]at [Eb]my [F]right [Bb]hand?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Place on the reliance;
[Cm]My [F]soul [Gm]with [F]courage [Bb]wait;
[Bb]His truth be thine affiance,
[Cm]When [F]faint [Gm]and [F]desolate.
[Bb]His might [Eb]thy [Dm]heart [Gm]shall strengthen,
[Cm/Eb]His [Bb/D]love thy [Cm]joy increase;
[Bb/D]Mercy [F]thy [Gm]days [Dm]shall lengthen;
[Eb]The [F]Lord [Bb/D]will [Eb]give [F]thee [Bb]peace.
{end_of_verse}
